From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Exclude the compiler loader from runtime-only builds

The compiler C API loader links against LLVM targets that only exist when
the compiler is built. Runtime-only builds with the Python bindings
include the compiler bindings directory and fail to link it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
diff --git a/compiler/bindings/c/CMakeLists.txt b/compiler/bindings/c/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/compiler/bindings/c/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/compiler/bindings/c/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -76,6 +76,9 @@
           iree::compiler::API::SharedImpl
       )
   endif()
+  if(NOT IREE_BUILD_COMPILER)
+    iree_cc_library_exclude_from_all(loader TRUE)
+  endif()
 else()
   # Dynamic library loading not available. Exclude loader from all.
   message(STATUS "Disabling compiler loader (platform does not support library loading)")
